1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,804
At 2 p.m., a Chinese office can suddenly go quiet.

2
00:00:05,154 --> 00:00:06,434
Lights off.

3
00:00:06,434 --> 00:00:07,830
Chairs back.

4
00:00:07,830 --> 00:00:11,553
Someone pulls out a folding bed.

5
00:00:11,903 --> 00:00:14,737
This is 午休 — wǔxiū — the lunch-break nap.

6
00:00:15,087 --> 00:00:20,617
In many Chinese schools and offices, the break is long enough for a short sleep —

7
00:00:20,617 --> 00:00:22,870
usually twenty to thirty minutes.

8
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:25,210
It's not laziness.

9
00:00:25,210 --> 00:00:30,958
Many people start early, commute far, and work late.

10
00:00:30,958 --> 00:00:32,837
A nap is a reset.

11
00:00:32,837 --> 00:00:35,490
The office doesn't stop.

12
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:37,148
It just pauses.

13
00:00:37,498 --> 00:00:41,712
In some schools, students sleep at their desks.

14
00:00:41,712 --> 00:00:46,196
In some offices, folding beds live under the desk.

15
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:48,208
Not everyone naps.

16
00:00:48,208 --> 00:00:53,010
But at the right time, the whole room can be asleep.

17
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:56,174
Does your office have a nap time?

